WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.171
If you were kidnaped and forced to play brutal
death games every night, what would you do?

00:00:05.213 --> 00:00:07.298
I'm here to break down the mistakes made,

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:12.512
what you should do, and how to beat the death
games in Alice in Borderland.

00:00:12.554 --> 00:00:17.100
This kid is about to realize that danger is around
every corner.

00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:22.147
This spiky haired student, Arisu,
wakes up on an empty beach with two other friends.

00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:27.235
They find themselves inside an overgrown city
where there are no signs of human life.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.282
Searching a convenience store, the reality begins
to sink in that they're in some sort of dream.

00:00:32.323 --> 00:00:33.700
Or so they think.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.871
Arisu tells the others that they've now
got the freedom to do whatever they want.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:41.458
But all this freedom will come at a deadly price.

00:00:41.499 --> 00:00:46.504
Later that night, the smoker Karube, begins
to worry that this dream isn't going to end.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:51.968
He urges the others to start taking the situation
seriously and stop the underage drinking.

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:55.805
There's no dream. They're far away from home
and they need to get back.

00:00:55.805 --> 00:00:57.098
That's when he hears something

00:00:57.098 --> 00:01:02.562
in the distance and realizes that they aren't
the only ones in this empty city. OK.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:07.525
If being in an abandoned city
sounds like a good idea, it may not seem so fun

00:01:07.525 --> 00:01:10.111
when we realize there's no Internet now.

00:01:10.111 --> 00:01:12.906
There's not much
we can do about waking up kidnaped.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.699
We have no idea where the hell we are,

00:01:14.699 --> 00:01:18.661
and there's a good chance that the other people
are going to try and hunt us down

00:01:18.661 --> 00:01:22.624
if other Japanese death games in general
are anything to go by.

00:01:22.665 --> 00:01:26.503
However, we first noticed that
right before we suddenly appeared here,

00:01:26.503 --> 00:01:31.716
there was a blast emitted from those fireworks
that seemingly blinded us for a period of time.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:36.137
However, we can clearly see now
and seemingly have no retinal damage,

00:01:36.137 --> 00:01:40.475
which means that the blast we saw
was clearly not some type of explosive ordinance.

00:01:40.475 --> 00:01:44.646
Since the blast from a one megaton
explosion would be bright enough to blind anyone

00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:49.692
who looks at it within a 53 mile radius,
because these kids were clearly

00:01:49.692 --> 00:01:54.614
within that radius, it's safe to say that
what they saw was clearly something else entirely.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:02:00.245
And also, we have no burns and are not suffering
from any type of acute radiation poisoning either,

00:02:00.245 --> 00:02:05.500
which if this scenario was caused by an explosion,
we likely would have at least felt something

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.085
burning on our skin by now.

00:02:07.085 --> 00:02:11.923
This means that putting aside any alien abduction
type crap, someone has put us here.

00:02:11.923 --> 00:02:15.760
At least that is what I would assume
based on all the current factors presented.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:21.057
This means that the only chilling I'd be doing
would be to crack open a cold one while we try

00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:24.227
and get to the bottom of this as soon as possible,
because I doubt

00:02:24.227 --> 00:02:29.732
anyone would kidnap us into having a good time
unless that spot was in Bangkok, Thailand.

00:02:29.732 --> 00:02:33.027
And in that case, I would
simply have called for help instead.

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:34.112
Or maybe I would.

00:02:34.112 --> 00:02:38.199
Yeah, probably not. Now, using regular survival
tips as a guessing guide.

00:02:38.199 --> 00:02:41.494
We can try our best to survive
as long as possible.

00:02:41.536 --> 00:02:45.165
The first thing we should do
is stock up on as much water as we can.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:49.252
Luckily for us, Japan's
tap water is completely safe to drink.

00:02:49.252 --> 00:02:51.671
In fact, it's some of the cleanest in the world.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.756
The next thing we should do is to look for food.

00:02:53.798 --> 00:02:57.343
Japan is a country known
for having large amounts of processed food,

00:02:57.343 --> 00:03:02.056
meaning the preservatives in said food should mean
that eating out won't be too difficult.

00:03:02.056 --> 00:03:06.519
Now that our basic essentials are sorted,
we still need to find out where the hell we are

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:10.940
and again, we seem to be fine
from a radiation standpoint, at least for now.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:16.279
But I would strip my boys down to their skivvies,
I mean underwear and check for any and all

00:03:16.279 --> 00:03:20.366
rope burns consisting of redness, irritation
or bleeding on the skin to indicate

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:23.953
if we were about at any point
during our time while unconscious,

00:03:23.953 --> 00:03:26.456
because either we've been kidnaped by some creep-o

00:03:26.497 --> 00:03:30.293
abducted by aliens,
or we are in some sick form of web purgatory.

00:03:30.293 --> 00:03:33.463
And if that's the case,
that means we're already dead.

00:03:33.463 --> 00:03:38.343
The boys find themselves at an overnight market
excited by all the amazing stalls

00:03:38.343 --> 00:03:39.677
available inside.

00:03:39.677 --> 00:03:44.682
They notice a booth in the middle of the market
mentioning that four entries have been confirmed

00:03:44.682 --> 00:03:49.854
over the loudspeaker worried Karube tells
the others to leave before anything bad happens,

00:03:49.854 --> 00:03:55.235
but that's when this mysterious lady interrupts
to warn him to not step outside.

00:03:55.276 --> 00:04:00.281
These kids look gullible as hell, and she comments
that they must be new around here.

00:04:00.323 --> 00:04:04.786
She says that the world they're in is very real
and death is around every corner.

00:04:04.827 --> 00:04:09.457
She flicks the kids cigaret out of the market,
and suddenly it disintegrates into nothing.

00:04:09.457 --> 00:04:14.003
The lady mentions that they're a part of a game,
and it's just about to begin.

00:04:14.045 --> 00:04:15.546
The booth announces that the games

00:04:15.546 --> 00:04:21.219
difficulty is set to three of clubs
and tells each person to draw one fortune slip.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:24.055
If everyone draws a fortune slip,
they beat the game.

00:04:24.055 --> 00:04:29.686
They win not to drawing a slip, though,
means that you fail before it even starts.

00:04:29.727 --> 00:04:33.106
The students demand that the lady reveals
everything she knows.

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:34.565
She introduces herself

00:04:34.565 --> 00:04:39.904
as Shibuki and tells them that the three of clubs
means that the game is less dangerous.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:44.617
The lady mentions that they need to be aware
of every small detail if they want to stay

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:49.247
alive, confused Arisu questions her
about the rules and where the hell they even are.

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:52.792
The lady gets angry
and tells him to figure it out himself.

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:55.878
They arrive at the booth
and the smoker decides to go first.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.548
He's given a slip that states You are the general.

00:04:58.548 --> 00:05:02.719
The person you're waiting for is south of here.
The next person to pick is Chota.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:07.056
He's given a mathematical equation
and ordered to write the answer down on this slip

00:05:07.056 --> 00:05:08.016
at the same time.

00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:12.895
Karube questions the lady asking her
why she's participating in another game.

00:05:12.937 --> 00:05:15.481
She tells them that they're all
in the same position

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:18.318
and doesn't know what will happen
after the game is over.

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:22.030
But that's when Chota answers
the mathematical equation wrong.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:26.326
The booth then announces that a wrong
answer will result in being shot dead.

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:29.871
Suddenly,
flaming arrows attack the kid and almost kill him.

00:05:29.871 --> 00:05:34.042
Shibuki tells them she'll go
next, and Arisu freaks his shit out at her.

00:05:34.083 --> 00:05:36.753
That's
when she mentions that there's a time limit.

00:05:36.794 --> 00:05:39.464
If all the lamps turn off, they'll lose the game.

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:42.216
Okay. This is some serious business.

00:05:42.216 --> 00:05:47.472
What we thought was a little fun game to keep us
occupied is actually going to result in our deaths

00:05:47.472 --> 00:05:48.806
if we don't do something.

00:05:48.806 --> 00:05:52.685
Now, looking at our options,
it doesn't seem like running is a good idea.

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:55.855
There's some sort of laser beam wall
covering our every direction,

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:58.524
and this is going to limit our escape
opportunities.

00:05:58.566 --> 00:06:03.071
Now we know if we get the mathematical equations
wrong, there's going to be flaming arrows

00:06:03.071 --> 00:06:06.699
ready to burn us alive
and shred us to pieces all at the same time.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:09.494
Great sense. There's no friends in this game.

00:06:09.494 --> 00:06:12.872
We should look to our buddies
and use this girl to our advantage.

00:06:12.914 --> 00:06:13.915
We don't know her

00:06:13.915 --> 00:06:18.503
and bringing more people along in our group
means that supplies will run out even faster.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:22.215
However, what we can do is use her body
as a sort of meat shield.

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:25.968
She doesn't look that small of a lady,
and I'm pretty sure Johnny Depp would agree.

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:30.431
And that means she's perfect for us
to use her as a shield from the arrows

00:06:30.431 --> 00:06:31.933
if we have to, of course.

00:06:31.933 --> 00:06:33.726
Now, we might not know how to beat

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:38.856
the game specifically, but what we do know
is that the game will end once the lamps burn out.

00:06:38.856 --> 00:06:42.193
The game never specifies
whether or not we can reignite them.

00:06:42.193 --> 00:06:46.656
So let's assume that we might be able to wait
out the game until they run out of flaming arrows.

00:06:46.656 --> 00:06:47.407
The lady did

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:53.246
tell us to pay attention to every small detail,
so this is probably our best chance of success.

00:06:53.329 --> 00:06:56.916
Shibuki picks her slip
and is given another problem.

00:06:56.999 --> 00:07:01.671
The lady tells the booth
her answer is throw, but she's completely wrong.

00:07:01.712 --> 00:07:05.174
Suddenly, hundreds of flaming arrows
are sent in their direction.

00:07:05.216 --> 00:07:09.971
Arisu becomes frozen with fear,
staring at a sea of death coming his way.

00:07:09.971 --> 00:07:14.559
His buddy runs over and kicks him in the back,
telling him to grow some balls and run.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:18.813
He then suddenly decides that he wants to live
and run safely to cover.

00:07:18.813 --> 00:07:22.400
But the group
then notices that Chota is still out in the open.

00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:26.195
He then gets struck in the calf by an arrow,
an Arisu goes to help.

00:07:26.195 --> 00:07:29.449
But he notices the curse
slip drop right next to him.

00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:32.952
Chota'ss leg catches on fire
and he screams out in pain.

00:07:32.994 --> 00:07:38.040
The smoker rushes over with a pool of water
and throws it onto his screaming friend

00:07:38.082 --> 00:07:41.419
outers, who praises his buddy for being a hero
and gets the courage

00:07:41.419 --> 00:07:43.463
to pick out the fourth and final slip.

00:07:43.504 --> 00:07:48.009
He draws the greatest curse, and the others
realize that they're done for others

00:07:48.009 --> 00:07:49.385
who begins to think hard.

00:07:49.385 --> 00:07:50.386
Looking back at all

00:07:50.386 --> 00:07:56.184
the recent events for any clues and suddenly
he blurts out the answer as 6.9 billion.

00:07:56.225 --> 00:08:01.772
The booth shows a number of 6.93 billion
and tells them that the answer is wrong.

00:08:01.772 --> 00:08:03.357
But Arisu has a plan.

00:08:03.357 --> 00:08:06.652
He turns around and tells
everyone that the question is impossible

00:08:06.652 --> 00:08:09.655
to answer to begin with.
Something is clearly wrong.

00:08:09.697 --> 00:08:12.241
The rules state
that they must answer the questions,

00:08:12.241 --> 00:08:14.911
but never mentioned that it would win them
the game.

00:08:14.911 --> 00:08:19.957
All they need to do is to avoid the arrows,
as clearly stated on every single slip

00:08:19.957 --> 00:08:21.626
they've been given so far.

00:08:21.626 --> 00:08:25.213
Seeing the arrows coming,
they grab cover and run as fast as possible.

00:08:25.213 --> 00:08:29.008
The group finds A well and Karube opens it
to find nothing but dirt.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:33.804
That's when he spots a tile like material
in the dirt and digs through to find a wheel.

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:38.351
They head underneath and the game
congratulates them for winning the three of clubs

00:08:38.351 --> 00:08:42.855
Arisu is given a visa showing him
how many days he can stay in the desolate city

00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:44.315
known as Borderland.

00:08:44.315 --> 00:08:49.153
Shibuki tells them that rumor states there are
a lot more people here than they realize.

00:08:49.195 --> 00:08:53.950
At night, they all appear in games
and your visa is extended if you win later.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:57.203
Chota spots a crazy man hiding in this school.

00:08:57.203 --> 00:08:59.080
The man blocks the door and mentions

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:02.416
that all his friends were killed
in the most horrifying ways possible.

00:09:02.416 --> 00:09:04.335
Suddenly, green beams hit the city

00:09:04.335 --> 00:09:09.131
and Arisu begins to realize the punishment
for their visas expiring.

00:09:09.131 --> 00:09:13.844
The next day, the group shares breakfast
and enjoys a little bit of peace and quiet.

00:09:13.844 --> 00:09:18.015
That's when Karube interrupts,
urging them to play another game tonight.

00:09:18.015 --> 00:09:20.893
He tells them
Chota will be sitting out since he's injured,

00:09:20.893 --> 00:09:24.522
but the others need to sharpen
their survival skills to make it out alive.

00:09:24.564 --> 00:09:28.776
Chota then says that since he's not playing,
his visas won't be expired.

00:09:28.859 --> 00:09:33.072
Shibuki volunteers to stay back with him,
and they agree to play another game

00:09:33.072 --> 00:09:34.323
when he's recovered

00:09:34.323 --> 00:09:39.495
the 2 enter the location for the second game
and see scary looking participants waiting around.

00:09:39.537 --> 00:09:44.417
A voice announces that the game has started and a
bloodthirsty killer is somewhere in the building.

00:09:44.458 --> 00:09:49.005
They're told the game that they're playing is tag,
and this complex is the playground.

00:09:49.046 --> 00:09:51.882
The difficulty is revealed to be five of spades.

00:09:51.882 --> 00:09:57.555
And this well-dressed man informs the boys
that speed based games require physical effort.

00:09:57.638 --> 00:10:00.141
The loudspeaker informs everyone that the game

00:10:00.141 --> 00:10:05.354
will last 30 minutes and whoever is
the killer will start hunting in 5 minutes.

00:10:05.396 --> 00:10:10.151
The complex has one room that isn't locked,
and that's the home base of the killer.

00:10:10.192 --> 00:10:14.113
If a player can reach the home base
within the time limit, they'll beat the game.

00:10:14.155 --> 00:10:18.284
The game is over when the time runs out
or all the players have been killed.

00:10:18.326 --> 00:10:19.869
Last but not least, though,

00:10:19.869 --> 00:10:23.831
the building is surrounded by landmines
to make sure no one leaves.

00:10:23.831 --> 00:10:26.208
Of course. OK, here we go again.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:27.126
We're now completely

00:10:27.126 --> 00:10:32.089
familiar with these types of death games
and know that some after shit is about to happen.

00:10:32.089 --> 00:10:35.217
People are going to die,
and there's no reason to be shocked.

00:10:35.259 --> 00:10:38.220
In fact, we need to use them to our advantage.

00:10:38.262 --> 00:10:39.430
We should try and pick out

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:44.644
any gullible suckers that we can use
and add them to our group of disposable idiots.

00:10:44.685 --> 00:10:48.606
There's some people here who are experiencing
these death games for the very first time,

00:10:48.648 --> 00:10:52.485
which means we can use their inexperience
to help them.

00:10:52.485 --> 00:10:56.322
If I was Arisu, I would tell the first timers
that were allowed to retry

00:10:56.322 --> 00:10:57.698
once were killed in the game.

00:10:57.698 --> 00:11:01.285
They've all just been transported to a random city
in the outskirts of Japan,

00:11:01.285 --> 00:11:05.414
and I know they're probably going to believe
anything that comes out of my mouth.

00:11:05.456 --> 00:11:06.415
This time around,

00:11:06.415 --> 00:11:11.170
it seems like whoever's making these games
is using landmines to keep us from running away.

00:11:11.212 --> 00:11:14.590
Really, this makes the situation
a lot easier for us to escape

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:17.677
rather than having instant death
laser beams all around us.

00:11:17.718 --> 00:11:21.472
That being said,
we don't know how many landmines have been planted

00:11:21.514 --> 00:11:25.726
or how far out of the landmines extend
or even where the hell they are.

00:11:25.726 --> 00:11:28.813
But I think it's safe to assume
that there's a lot of them.

00:11:28.854 --> 00:11:33.275
Let's just completely forget about the objective
of the game and try our hand at escaping.

00:11:33.275 --> 00:11:37.863
We don't know if this Visa stuff is even real,
and it sure doesn't seem like throwing ourselves

00:11:37.863 --> 00:11:40.491
into more death
games is the best way to stay alive.

00:11:40.533 --> 00:11:45.037
Arisu and Karube are best off
convincing some dumb schmucks to test it out

00:11:45.037 --> 00:11:48.874
and throw themselves out of bounds
to their purely coincidental death.

00:11:48.916 --> 00:11:53.421
I'd use my trusty friend Karube
and tell him to lead the way as another lifeline.

00:11:53.462 --> 00:11:56.090
However, that would it mean we're in the clear
just yet.

00:11:56.132 --> 00:11:58.259
It's safe to assume that these game creators

00:11:58.259 --> 00:12:01.011
have more than a few landmines
planted around the area,

00:12:01.011 --> 00:12:03.180
which means
while other people are getting massacred,

00:12:03.222 --> 00:12:06.600
if we can find a heavy object,
something like a fire extinguisher

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:09.061
which is commonly found in apartment complexes,

00:12:09.061 --> 00:12:12.481
we could throw that off of the building as well
and on the surrounding area.

00:12:12.523 --> 00:12:16.736
This will detonate at the land mines
and give us a clear pathway out of here, possibly.

00:12:16.777 --> 00:12:19.447
Of course,
this isn't a foolproof method of surviving,

00:12:19.447 --> 00:12:21.824
but thinking out of the box
is more important to it.

00:12:21.866 --> 00:12:23.743
Our lives are on the line.

00:12:23.743 --> 00:12:26.996
Arisu
instantly begins analyzing the situation at hand.

00:12:27.037 --> 00:12:30.374
Suddenly they hear the sound of a door opening
and shots are fired.

00:12:30.416 --> 00:12:33.794
They run upstairs to see two players
being brutally murdered.

00:12:33.836 --> 00:12:38.382
The killer turns to them and starts shooting,
forcing them to run for their lives.

00:12:38.424 --> 00:12:39.717
Arisu stops his buddy

00:12:39.717 --> 00:12:44.013
and tells them to head another direction,
using the well-dressed man as a decoy.

00:12:44.013 --> 00:12:44.680
And he tells

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:49.643
Karube to hold his breath once the killer
passes, the boys run as fast as possible away.

00:12:49.685 --> 00:12:52.813
That's when Arisu reveals
that the killer was dragging his foot,

00:12:52.813 --> 00:12:54.899
meaning they can move faster than him.

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:58.569
Arisu tells his buddy
that now's the time to find the home base.

00:12:58.611 --> 00:13:01.113
Karube screams out to the other players,
telling them

00:13:01.113 --> 00:13:03.866
the identity of the killer
and urges them to help each other.

00:13:03.908 --> 00:13:07.828
However, he doesn't realize
that this is not a game of trust.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:12.708
This purple haired girl tries to warn this player
about the killer, but gives up and climbs away.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:14.585
Narrowly missing the machine gun.

00:13:14.585 --> 00:13:19.465
Meanwhile, this desparate man tries
to leave the play area and gets blown to bits,

00:13:19.465 --> 00:13:22.384
assuring the others
that there's no reason to leave yet.

00:13:22.426 --> 00:13:23.219
Now, 10

00:13:23.219 --> 00:13:28.390
minutes have passed and they've begun to realize
that checking each door manually is too slow.

00:13:28.432 --> 00:13:32.353
Arisu spaces out for a second
and the killer spots them standing around.

00:13:32.394 --> 00:13:36.148
He then hides behind the wall,
hoping that the killer only noticed his body.

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:40.694
Karube runs down stairs and bumps into these two
serious looking players.

00:13:40.736 --> 00:13:44.740
They tell him that they're looking for the killer
and it's time to start running.

00:13:44.824 --> 00:13:47.743
Karube grabs
the killer's attention, distracting him

00:13:47.743 --> 00:13:50.204
while the others spray their fire extinguishers.

00:13:50.246 --> 00:13:52.081
That's when they signaled to the bald man,

00:13:52.081 --> 00:13:55.209
and he opens the elevator door
to choke him out from behind.

00:13:55.209 --> 00:13:59.171
But suddenly the bald man is shot dead
and the killer reveals another gun,

